  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 204 PM EDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nDaily Storm Chances and a Gradual Warming Trend:\n\nNorth and Central Georgia will remain in moist southwest flow \nthrough mid-week as a cutoff mid-level low sits over the TN Valley. \nFrom late week into the weekend, model guidance is in pretty good \nagreement on the pattern slightly shifting as the low gets kicked \nout by a ridge building in from over the Atlantic. Overall, this \npattern will support fairly typical summer weather, with scattered \nto numerous afternoon showers and storms each day of the upcoming \nweek. High temperatures will initially be in the 80s to low 90s mid-\nweek due to increased cloud cover and proximity of the mid-level \nlow, but will gradually warm up to the low to mid 90s by the weekend \nas the ridge builds in.",
